{"path":"regex/regex_token_iterator/operator_arith","title":"std::regex_token_iterator<BidirIt,CharT,Traits>::operator++, operator++(int)","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::regex_token_iterator&lt;BidirIt,CharT,Traits&gt;::</span>operator++, operator++<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">(int)</span>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/regex/regex_token_iterator/operator_arith","section":"regex","kind":"page","summary":"Advances the iterator on the next sub match.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">regex_token_iterator<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> operator<span class=\"sy2\">++</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">regex_token_iterator operator<span class=\"sy2\">++</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Advances the iterator on the next sub match.\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: Explain better. For example, <code>subs</code> is an exposition-only vector of matched sub-expressions. </div>\n<p>If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code> is a suffix iterator, sets <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code> to an end-of-sequence iterator.\n</p><p>Otherwise, if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">N <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> <span class=\"nu0\">1</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> subs.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>, increments N and sets result to the address of the current match.\n</p><p>Otherwise, sets <code>N</code> to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span></code> and increments <code>position</code>. If <code>position</code> is not an end-of-sequence iterator the operator sets result to the address of the current match.\n</p><p>Otherwise, if any of the values stored in subs is equal to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span></span></code> and <span class=\"t-cc\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">prev<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>suffix<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>.<span class=\"me1\">length</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></span> is not <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span></code> the operator sets <code>*this</code> to a suffix iterator that points to the range [<code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">prev<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>suffix<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>.<span class=\"me1\">first</span></span></code>, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">prev<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>suffix<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>.<span class=\"me1\">second</span></span></code>).\n</p><p>Otherwise, sets <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code> to an end-of-sequence iterator.\n</p><p>The behavior is undefined if the iterator is end-of-sequence iterator.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code></div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> The previous value of the iterator.</div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"regex","title":"Regular expressions library (since C++11)"},{"path":"regex/regex_token_iterator","title":"std::regex_token_iterator"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::regex_token_iterator<BidirIt,CharT,Traits>::operator++, operator++(int)","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++11. Advances the iterator on the next sub match."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Return value","note":"*this"}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":154,"codeBlockCount":0}
